    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "## Household review complete\n\n- **Northwind Outfitters:** Submitted a refund-to-original-payment return request for **$180.77** (order NW-59004). Confirmation **NW-R1001**. You\u2019ll need to print the label and ship the jacket; a follow-up is scheduled for October 24, ahead of the November 1 return deadline.\n- **Summit Card:** Submitted a courtesy request to reverse the **$95** annual fee. Confirmation **SC-1002**; a follow-up is scheduled for October 24.\n- **St Mary Hospital:** The **$5,996.01** uninsured ER bill may qualify for financial assistance. I asked for household size and current annual household income, which are needed to proceed. I also noted the need for an itemized bill.\n- **Keystone EOB:** A separate **$1,364.87** claim was denied for missing prior authorization. The stated 180-day appeal deadline is **December 27, 2026**. A formal appeal needs your approval because it shares health information.\n- **QuickLoan settlement:** The July 31, 2026 claim deadline has passed, and no matching QuickLoan charge appeared in the available transactions.\n- **Recurring charges:** Spotify is **$11.99/month**, rent is **$1,725/month**, and Metro Power varies with usage. The records don\u2019t show these are unwanted or identify a clear utility price increase, so no service changes were requested.\n- **Job loss:** I saved a note to check benefit options such as SNAP, LIHEAP, and unemployment assistance.\n\nThe Northwind and Summit requests are submitted; no refunds have posted yet. The remaining follow-ups are the hospital facts and the health appeal approval.",
    "committed_micros": 79587
